  "faithful": "In the time of the Romans, the inhabitants of Cappadocia bore fo bad a character, and were reputed fo vicious and lewd, that, among the neighbouring nations, a wicked man was emphatically called a Cappadocian. In after ages, however, their lewd difposition was fo corrected and refrained by the pure doctrines of Christianity, that no country whatever has produced greater champions of the Christian religion, or given to the church prelates of more unblemished characters.",
